# FastAPI Backend Best Practices

- Use Pydantic models for request/response validation and type hints throughout.
- Prefer dependency injection for shared resources; inject `QueryService` via `Depends(get_query_service)`.
- Initialize app-wide resources in FastAPI lifespan (startup/shutdown), not at import time.
- Register exception handlers once in `create_app`.
- Use appropriate HTTP status codes and return shapes.
- Log with `logging` (no prints) and preserve exception chains (see [exception-chaining.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/exception-chaining.mdc)).

## Codebase references
- App factory and lifespan: [backend/app/main.py](mdc:backend/app/main.py)
- DI helper: [backend/app/dependencies.py](mdc:backend/app/dependencies.py)
- Validation and handlers: [backend/app/core/validation.py](mdc:backend/app/core/validation.py)
- Unified service: [backend/app/services/query_service.py](mdc:backend/app/services/query_service.py)

## Router guidance
- Always import `get_query_service` where `Depends(get_query_service)` is used.
- Avoid file-scoped singletons inside routers; use DI to access app-scoped state.

## Handlers
- Let `HTTPException` and `ValidationError` propagate to their handlers.
- Wrap unexpected exceptions into 500 responses centrally; avoid duplicating try/except in each route.
